This patch series implements the Purge UE procedure in the MME according to
3GPP TS 24.301 and TS 29.272 specifications.

Overview:
When the Implicit Detach timer expires, the MME should send a Purge-UE-Request
to the HSS before removing the UE context. The HSS marks the UE as "purged",
ensuring fresh authentication vectors are generated on the next attach.

Key features implemented:
1. Purge-UE-Request (PUR) transmission during Implicit Detach
2. PUR transmission even after S1 connection has been released
3. Automatic bearer status mismatch correction during TAU (Tracking Area Update)
4. State management with purge_ue_in_progress flag
5. Robust error handling for edge cases (enb_ue absence, timer races)
6. Timer adjustments for faster testing (optional)

Implementation highlights:
- 6 bugs identified and fixed during staged implementation
- Full 3GPP compliance (TS 24.301 §5.3.5, TS 29.272 §7.2.14)
- Backward compatible - no breaking changes to existing functionality
- Asynchronous PUR processing with proper state management
- Comprehensive documentation in both Japanese and English (1,769 lines each)

Technical changes:
- Added purge_ue_in_progress flag to mme_ue_t structure
- Added ue_pdn_status_mismatch flag to mme_sess_t structure
- Made enb_ue parameter optional in mme_s6a_send_pur() and mme_s6a_pua_cb()
- Enhanced TAU processing to detect and auto-correct bearer state mismatches
- Modified implicit detach timer handling to trigger PUR before session cleanup

Test coverage:
- Implicit Detach with enb_ue present (normal case)
- Implicit Detach with enb_ue absent (S1 already released)
- TAU with bearer status mismatch
- PUR/PUA message exchange validation
- HSS purge_flag verification

